{"content":[{"c":["HAROD"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Spring beside which Gideon and his army camped before their encounter with the Midianites (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.7.1","r":"Judg.7.1","rawR":"Judg.7.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.7.1","value":"Judg.7.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 7:1"},"). Perhaps this is the same spring by which Saul and his army pitched their tents prior to their battle with the Philistines (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.29.1","r":"1Sam.29.1","rawR":"1Sam.29.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.29.1","value":"1Sam.29.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 29:1"},"). The spring of Harod is at ‘Ain Jalud by the northern side of Mt Gilboa, about two miles (3.2 kilometers) southeast of Zerin."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Home of Shammah and Elika, two of David’s valiant warriors (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.23.25","r":"2Sam.23.25","rawR":"2Sam.23.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.23.25","value":"2Sam.23.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 23:25"},"). In the parallel passage (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.11.27","r":"1Chr.11.27","rawR":"1Chr.11.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.11.27","value":"1Chr.11.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 11:27"},"), Elika’s name is omitted and Shammah (Shammoth) is listed as a Harorite instead of a Harodite. “Harorite” reflects a later scribal error where the copyist mistook the Hebrew letter “d” for an “r.”"],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Harod","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jgs 7:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.7.1","rawQueryValue":"Judg.7.1","sourceRefExact":"Judg.7.1"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 29:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.29.1","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.29.1","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.29.1"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 23:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.23.25","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.23.25","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.23.25"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 11:27","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.11.27","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.11.27","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.11.27"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"cf94f00c996d8d684a2727eb376680d0e7f74bf4196ac7e230ced6161e861acb","sourceItemName":"Harod","sourceItemOrder":122,"sourceMember":"Articles/H.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Harod","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Harod","title":"Harod","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}